From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Add pcie_acs_override boot parameter for P2P through
 PLX switches

X99-E WS uses PLX PEX8747 switches whose ACS (Access Control Services)
blocks peer-to-peer DMA between GPUs on different downstream ports.
The kernel P2PDMA subsystem checks ACS independently of IOMMU mode, so
even with iommu=pt the pci_p2pdma_distance() rejects the P2P path:

  amdgpu: PCIe P2P access from peer device ... is not supported by the chipset

Add a boot parameter 'pcie_acs_override=' accepting comma-separated
values:

  downstream    - override ACS on PCIe switch downstream ports
  multifunction - override ACS on multifunction endpoints

When the override matches, the quirk reports all requested ACS flags
as satisfied, allowing the P2PDMA subsystem to approve P2P paths
through the affected bridges.

WARNING: This disables ACS isolation which is a security boundary when
IOMMU is in strict mode.  Only safe with iommu=pt (passthrough) where
DMA isolation is already disabled.

Based on the well-known out-of-tree ACS override design originally
proposed for VFIO GPU passthrough use cases.

[YANG JOO WOONG: written for v6.18.24, X99 PLX PEX8747 + RDNA4 GPU P2P]

Signed-off-by: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -5059,6 +5059,50 @@ static int  pci_quirk_wangxun_nic_acs(struct pci_dev *dev, u16 acs_flags)
 	return false;
 }

+static bool acs_override_downstream;
+static bool acs_override_multifunction;
+
+static int __init pcie_acs_override_setup(char *p)
+{
+	if (!p)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	while (*p) {
+		if (!strncmp(p, "downstream", 10)) {
+			acs_override_downstream = true;
+		} else if (!strncmp(p, "multifunction", 13)) {
+			acs_override_multifunction = true;
+		}
+		p += strcspn(p, ",");
+		if (*p == ',')
+			p++;
+	}
+
+	if (acs_override_downstream || acs_override_multifunction)
+		pr_warn("pcie_acs_override: ACS isolation disabled for%s%s\n",
+			acs_override_downstream ? " downstream-ports" : "",
+			acs_override_multifunction ? " multifunction" : "");
+
+	return 0;
+}
+early_param("pcie_acs_override", pcie_acs_override_setup);
+
+static int pci_quirk_acs_override(struct pci_dev *dev, u16 acs_flags)
+{
+	if (acs_override_downstream &&
+	    pci_pcie_type(dev) == PCI_EXP_TYPE_DOWNSTREAM)
+		return pci_acs_ctrl_enabled(acs_flags,
+			PCI_ACS_SV | PCI_ACS_TB | PCI_ACS_RR |
+			PCI_ACS_CR | PCI_ACS_UF | PCI_ACS_DT);
+
+	if (acs_override_multifunction && dev->multifunction)
+		return pci_acs_ctrl_enabled(acs_flags,
+			PCI_ACS_SV | PCI_ACS_TB | PCI_ACS_RR |
+			PCI_ACS_CR | PCI_ACS_UF | PCI_ACS_DT);
+
+	return -ENOTTY;
+}
+
 static const struct pci_dev_acs_enabled {
 	u16 vendor;
 	u16 device;
@@ -5227,6 +5271,8 @@ static const struct pci_dev_acs_enabled {
 	/* Wangxun nics */
 	{ PCI_VENDOR_ID_WANGXUN, PCI_ANY_ID, pci_quirk_wangxun_nic_acs },
+	/* pcie_acs_override boot parameter -- catch-all, must be last */
+	{ PCI_ANY_ID, PCI_ANY_ID, pci_quirk_acs_override },
 	{ 0 }
 };

